// Real Ghidra 12.0.4 ground-truth output for an x86-64 freestanding ELF
// whose every public function executes one x86-64 synchronization
// instruction (MFENCE / LFENCE / SFENCE / PAUSE) or LOCK-prefixed RMW
// (XADD / CMPXCHG / XCHG / INC / DEC / OR). Source:
// firmwares/atomics-probe/atomics_probe_x86_64.c.
//
// Stock Ghidra emits only LOCK and UNLOCK as CALLOTHER intrinsic targets
// (the SLEIGH define-pcodeop list in
// Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/lockable.sinc declares no others).
// The fence and pause instructions lower to inline P-Code with no
// CALLOTHER target at all -- they are visible only as the disassembled
// mnemonics in the probe function bodies.
//
// The normalizer intentionally has no x86 entry: there is no userop to
// canonicalize. LOCK and UNLOCK fall through to the registered FunctionDecl
// path verbatim. This fixture documents the production reality.

// LOCK / UNLOCK markers pass through unchanged:
// CIR-DAG: @LOCK
// CIR-DAG: @UNLOCK
// LL-DAG: call {{.*}} @LOCK
// LL-DAG: call {{.*}} @UNLOCK
